\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The three-layer verification stack. ProVerif (top) discharges design-level obligations against a Dolev--Yao adversary. Kani (middle) closes the \emph  {specification gap}: the same properties, restated as Rust source-level claims on the \texttt  {harbor-card-rs} crate, are discharged by bounded model checking. Runtime conformance tests (bottom) close the \emph  {deployment gap}: the FFI-bridged binary is exercised with the formally verified attack vectors. Cinnabar arrows show obligations flowing down (what each lower layer must preserve); teal arrows show evidence flowing back up (what each lower layer actually delivers). The stack is sound only if every bridge holds.}}{11}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:anchor-verification-stack}{{7}{11}{The three-layer verification stack. ProVerif (top) discharges design-level obligations against a Dolev--Yao adversary. Kani (middle) closes the \emph {specification gap}: the same properties, restated as Rust source-level claims on the \texttt {harbor-card-rs} crate, are discharged by bounded model checking. Runtime conformance tests (bottom) close the \emph {deployment gap}: the FFI-bridged binary is exercised with the formally verified attack vectors. Cinnabar arrows show obligations flowing down (what each lower layer must preserve); teal arrows show evidence flowing back up (what each lower layer actually delivers). The stack is sound only if every bridge holds}{figure.caption.14}{}}
